        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the inpatient treatment of your patient, a 73-year-old female, admitted on 17.12.2025 due to acute exacerbation of known COPD. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive measures. Clinical condition improved satisfactorily. At discharge, oxygen saturation was stable on room air. Pulmonary rehabilitation and optimisation of inhaled maintenance therapy were recommended. Please arrange follow-up including spirometry. Should you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact me.</div>"
            },
